<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Mpondomise Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1600 CE – 1880 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A southern Nguni kingdom of the eastern Cape whose last independent king, Mhlontlo, led a revolt against Cape rule in 1880.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mpondomise">Mpondomise</a> share their earliest royal genealogy with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mpondo">Mpondo</a>, from whom they separated many generations before written records. By the 17th century they occupied the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mzimvubu-river">Mzimvubu</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsitsa-river">Tsitsa</a> valleys, around modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsolo">Tsolo</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qumbu">Qumbu</a> in the eastern Cape.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Kings ruled through royal kin and councillors over chiefdoms of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a>-herding and cereal-farming homesteads. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mpondomise">Mpondomise</a> were renowned as rainmakers and were respected by neighbouring peoples for their ritual standing. In the 19th century they were caught between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mpondo">Mpondo</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thembu">Thembu</a> and incoming <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mfengu">Mfengu</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sotho-people">Sotho</a> groups, and the kingdom was often divided between rival branches.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mhlontlo">Mhlontlo</a> accepted a Cape magistrate in 1873, but in 1880 his followers killed the magistrate Hamilton Hope and rose in revolt. The rising was crushed, Mhlontlo fled to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/basutoland">Basutoland</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mpondomise">Mpondomise</a> lands were absorbed into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/cape-colony">Cape Colony</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1600 CE – 1880 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central and Southern Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:91.54%;width:5.57%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1600 CE – 1880 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Mhlontlo</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Traditional Xhosa religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>isiXhosa</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/south-africa">South Africa</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>amaMpondomise</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1740&amp;focus=mpondomise-kingdom" aria-label="Mpondomise Kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5292 3276 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Mpondomise Kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5470 3663h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5612 3532h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5612 3532h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day South Africa. <a href="/atlas?year=1740&amp;focus=mpondomise-kingdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
